{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Implicit-PC IF FIFO implementation notes\n\n- Changed `rtl/if_stage.sv` to remove the queued PC payload registers\n  (`pc0_q` and `pc1_q`). The FIFO still stores `instr0_q`, `instr1_q`, and\n  `count_q` exactly as before.\n- The decode-side PC is now derived from `fetch_pc_q - (count_q << 2)` when\n  the FIFO is non-empty. Empty bypass still reports `fetch_pc_q` directly.\n- Redirect behavior, imem push qualification, decode pop qualification, and\n  instruction shift/count transitions were otherwise left unchanged.\n- Deviation from the hypothesis: the derived PC is expressed as one shifted\n  count delta rather than a two-way `count == 1 ? -4 : -8` mux, to keep the\n  arithmetic compact while preserving the same count-1/count-2 behavior.\n- Concern: this removes the wide PC queue flops but does add a small\n  fetch_pc/count subtract on the IF-to-ID PC path. It is expected to be less\n  damaging than the old redirect/pop-driven PC payload register muxes, but\n  final Gowin timing is the real arbiter.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- Verilator lint: pass\n  `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n  Note: the literal `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaulted the harness to\n  `NRET=2` and failed to compile against this `nret: 1` core before\n  simulation. The orchestrator path normally injects the value from\n  `core.yaml`; the rerun above matches that contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
