{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Bypass generic ALU for adds\n\n- Changed `rtl/ex_stage.sv` so ADD, ADDI-style `rs1+imm`, SUB, and AUIPC writeback results are selected from dedicated carry-chain arithmetic paths before falling back to the generic ALU.\n- Reused the existing `rs1+imm` fast adder for ADDI, load/store address generation, and JALR target calculation. Added direct `rs1+rs2`, `rs1-rs2`, `pc+imm`, and `pc+4` paths in EX.\n- Changed `rtl/alu.sv` so the generic ALU no longer implements `ALU_ADD` or `ALU_SUB` in hardware mode; it remains responsible for logic, shifts, comparisons, LUI, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS M-operation substitutes.\n- Updated `test/test_alu.py` to match the narrowed generic ALU contract. Architectural ADD/SUB behavior is now covered at the pipeline/formal/cosim level rather than by the standalone ALU unit.\n\nDeviations:\n- Kept the existing ALU opcode encodings and decoder behavior unchanged. The bypass is entirely in EX-stage result selection.\n- Did not change RVFI, pipeline depth, stall behavior, or forwarding policy.\n\nConcerns:\n- The bypass adds a few parallel arithmetic results in EX. The intended tradeoff is a shorter ADD/ADDI/SUB/AUIPC writeback cone at the cost of some extra carry-chain area.\n- A bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` built the harness with its default `NRET=2` and failed before simulation because this core correctly exposes only the `nret: 1` RVFI port set. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches `core.yaml` and passed.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_alu.py`: pass.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented. The EX stage now bypasses the generic ALU for `ADD`, `ADDI`-style `rs1+imm`, `SUB`, and `AUIPC`; `alu.sv` is narrowed to non-add operations plus ALTOPS M stand-ins. Updated `test_alu.py` and wrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nVerification:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Formal: pass, 53/53\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_alu.py`: pass\n\nNote: bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` still builds with default `NRET=2` and fails before simulation; `core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`, so `NRET=1` is the matching local invocation."}}
