{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,140p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## What changed\n\n- Made `hazard_unit.sv` operand-role aware for load-use stalls. The next instruction now stalls only when the pending load feeds an EX-stage operand: R-type/branch rs1 or rs2, I/load/JALR rs1, and store base rs1. Store rs2 data and non-source bitfields in I/U/J/fence/system-style encodings no longer force a bubble.\n- Added a late WB-to-MEM forwarding path in `mem_stage.sv`. A store in MEM can replace its write data with the current WB-stage value when `rs2_addr` matches, and the same path repairs retired `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` for RVFI source reporting.\n- Stopped EX/MEM forwarding from treating loads as having forwardable data; load results are only forwarded from MEM/WB/WB data.\n- Added focused cocotb pipeline cases covering load-to-store-data no-bubble forwarding, store-base/ALU/branch dependencies that still stall, and an OP-IMM false rs2 hazard with RVFI source-data repair.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- I added the focused tests to `test_pipeline.py` instead of creating a separate `test_load_store_forward.py`, reusing the existing core harness and instruction encoders.\n- The MEM-stage bypass forwards any WB-stage register write that matches the store/source register, not only loads. This keeps the logic simple and also preserves correct RVFI source values for raw bitfields after any immediately older writer.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- The added WB compare/mux sits on the store-data/RVFI-source side of MEM as intended. It should not touch the branch redirect path.\n- Local `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults the harness to `NRET=2` unless `NRET` is supplied, despite this core declaring `nret: 1`; the initial plain invocation failed at C++ compile time looking for `_1` RVFI ports. Rerunning with `NRET=1` passed.\n\n## Local status\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Cocotb pipeline test: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
