{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"The bug class is clearer now: a dependent instruction can sit in `ID/EX` for more than one cycle. It sees the MEM/WB forward on the first EX attempt, but if the stage is held, the MEM/WB window moves on and the stale `ID/EX.rs1_val` comes back. I’m checking which hold path caused it before choosing the smallest architectural fix."}}
