{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"module if_stage|if_stage\" cores/bench -S'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/rtl/core.sv:104:  if_stage u_if (\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:1:// rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:15:module if_stage (\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:74:  // IF -> ID combinational bundle (no register; PC reg sits in if_stage).\ncores/bench/test/test_direct_jal_predictor.py:137:            \"if_stage.sv\", \"id_stage.sv\", \"ex_stage.sv\",\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:381:            \"if_stage.sv\", \"id_stage.sv\", \"ex_stage.sv\",\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static BTFN fetch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline fetches sequentially and resolves every taken branch or\\njump in EX, forcing wrong-path instructions to be flushed. CoreMark contains\\ntight loops and frequent unconditional JAL control flow, so the always-not-\\ntaken policy pays the redirect penalty repeatedly on hot backward branches\\nand calls even when their targets are immediate constants available at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline fetches sequentially and resolves every taken branch or\\njump in EX, forcing wrong-path instructions to be flushed. CoreMark contains\\ntight loops and frequent unconditional JAL control flow, so the always-not-\\ntaken policy pays the redirect penalty repeatedly on hot backward branches\\nand calls even when their targets are immediate constants available at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small static predictor in IF that decodes only enough of io_imemData to\\nrecognize conditional branches with negative B-immediates and unconditional\\nJAL instructions. Fetch should set the next PC to the predicted target for\\nbackward branches and all JALs, carry the predicted next PC through ID/EX, and\\nlet EX redirect only when the actual next PC differs from the prediction.\\nCorrectly predicted loop backedges and JALs then avoid the two younger\\nwrong-path bubbles, while forward branches and JALR keep the existing\\ncorrection behavior. The added IF decode/adder is small compared with the\\ncurrent ALU/forw\n…[92231 of 95303 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d5bcb7848bf0e80c]…\n83, \"delta_pct\": -2.89, \"vs_baseline\": 1136.22, \"fmax_mhz\": 63.556, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4242013, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3044, \"ff\": 953, \"seeds\": [60.836, 63.556, 63.556], \"perturbations\": [[0, 60.836, 14], [1, 63.556, 14], [2, 63.556, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc1_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -11.438, \"arrival_ns\": 21.732, \"logic_cells\": 21, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T15:02:50.639112Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r12s2 (regression, -2.89%): Extending the metadata-free direct-JAL decode redirect to conditional branches regressed because `bp_pc`/`bp_instr` compares, redirect-target muxing, and an ID/EX `predicted_branch_taken` repair bit put predictor metadata back on the fragile decode-to-IF/EX control path.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
