{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Tiny direct-mapped I-cache\n\nChanged `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv` to add a 32-entry direct-mapped\ninstruction cache in front of the existing two-entry fetch FIFO. Each line\nstores one 32-bit instruction plus a valid bit and PC tag. The fetch path now\ntreats either an I-cache hit or `imem_ready` as a valid fetch source; misses\ncontinue to retry the same PC until `imem_ready` fills the selected cache line.\n\nRedirects still flush only the IF queue and restart `fetch_pc_q`; cache valid\nbits, tags, and data are retained. I used 32 entries rather than 64 to keep\nthe hit compare and data mux smaller on the fragile IF path.\n\nAdded `cores/bench/test/test_icache.py`, a standalone cocotb test for\nhit-under-imem-stall, miss retry/fill, redirect queue flush with retained\ncache contents, and repeated cached loop fetches while imem is stalled.\n\nConcerns: the hit check is now on the decode-facing IF path and the cache adds\nstate, so Fmax may drop. The formal `reg_ch0` check became noticeably slower\nthan before, which is expected from the extra cache state.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `python3 -m pytest cores/bench/test/test_icache.py -q`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: local build failed before simulation because the bare Makefile path defaulted the harness to `NRET=2` while this core declares `nret: 1`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/test/test_icache.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/test/test_icache.py\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Focused tests for the IF-stage direct-mapped instruction cache.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.clock import Clock\nfrom cocotb.triggers import RisingEdge, Timer\n\nfrom _helpers import run_cocotb\n\n\nINSN0 = 0x00100093  # addi x1, x0, 1\nINSN1 = 0x00200113  # addi x2, x0, 2\nINSN2 = 0x00300193  # addi x3, x0, 3\nBAD   = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n\ndef _out(dut) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Return (valid, pc, instr) from packed if_id_t output.\"\"\"\n    raw = int(dut.out.value)\n    valid = raw & 0x1\n    instr = (raw >> 1) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    pc = (raw >> 33) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return valid, pc, instr\n\n\nasync def _reset(dut) -> None:\n    cocotb.start_soon(Clock(dut.clock, 10, \"ns\").start())\n    dut.reset.value = 1\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.decode_pop.value = 0\n    dut.redirect.value = 0\n    dut.redirect_target.value = 0\n    dut.decode_jal_redirect.value = 0\n    dut.decode_jal_redirect_target.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = 0\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    dut.reset.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\nasync def _fetch_ready(dut, instr: int, pop: int = 1) -> None:\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 1\n    dut.imem_data.value = instr\n    dut.decode_pop.value = pop\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\nasync def _redirect_to(dut, pc: int) -> None:\n    dut.redirect.value = 1\n    dut.redirect_target.value = pc\n    dut.decode_pop.value = 0\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    dut.redirect.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def cache_hit_serves_when_imem_stalled(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN0)\n    assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == 4\n\n    await _redirect_to(dut, 0)\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = BAD\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n    valid, pc, instr = _out(dut)\n    assert (valid, pc, instr) == (1, 0, INSN0)\n\n    dut.decode_pop.value = 1\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == 4\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def miss_retries_until_ready_and_then_fills(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = BAD\n    dut.decode_pop.value = 1\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n        valid, pc, _ = _out(dut)\n        assert valid == 0 and pc == 0\n        assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == 0\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN0)\n    assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == 4\n\n    await _redirect_to(dut, 0)\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = BAD\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert _out(dut) == (1, 0, INSN0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def redirect_flushes_queue_but_keeps_cache_line(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n\n    dut.decode_pop.value = 0\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN0, pop=0)\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN1, pop=0)\n    valid, pc, instr = _out(dut)\n    assert (valid, pc, instr) == (1, 0, INSN0)\n\n    await _redirect_to(dut, 4)\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = BAD\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n    valid, pc, instr = _out(dut)\n    assert (valid, pc, instr) == (1, 4, INSN1)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def cached_loop_fetches_through_imem_stalls(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN0)\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN1)\n    await _fetch_ready(dut, INSN2)\n    assert int(dut.imem_addr.value) == 12\n\n    await _redirect_to(dut, 0)\n    dut.imem_ready.value = 0\n    dut.imem_data.value = BAD\n\n    seen = []\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n        seen.append(_out(dut))\n        dut.decode_pop.value = 1\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n\n    assert seen == [\n        (1, 0, INSN0),\n        (1, 4, INSN1),\n        (1, 8, INSN2),\n    ]\n\n\ndef test_icache_runner():\n    run_cocotb(\n        toplevel=\"if_stage\",\n        sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"if_stage.sv\"],\n        test_module=\"test_icache\",\n    )\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
