{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m going to keep the common ALU free of real `*`/`/`/`%`, put all M arithmetic behind a small ready/done unit, and let the EX stage emit bubbles while that unit is running. The important bit is that an older MEM instruction can still drain once when an M op starts, but no incomplete M result reaches EX/MEM."}}
