{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Split execute with operand latch implementation notes\n\nChanged:\n- Added an `exa_exb_t` operand bundle in `rtl/core_pkg.sv`.\n- Reworked `rtl/ex_stage.sv` into EXA/EXB: EXA latches post-forward operands, immediates, control, PC, rd/source metadata, instruction bits, and valid; EXB runs the existing ALU, branch/jump target logic, load/store address generation, and RV32M unit into the existing EX/MEM register.\n- Retargeted forwarding so EXA can take the current EXB result, EX/MEM ALU result, or MEM/WB writeback data. EX/MEM load results are excluded from ready forwarding.\n- Expanded hazard handling for the extra execute substage: redirects flush younger ID/EX and EXA work, load consumers wait until load data is available at MEM/WB, and fetched load-dependent instructions are kept out of ID/EX to avoid stale held operands.\n- Wired the new EXA metadata and bubble signal through `rtl/core.sv`.\n\nDeviations:\n- No new modules were added. The split is contained in the existing `ex_stage` plus updated hazard/forward units.\n- Load-use latency is conservative: fetched consumers of loads in EXA or EX/MEM are bubbled until the load reaches MEM/WB rather than adding a MEM-stage load-data bypass.\n\nConcerns:\n- The extra load-use bubbles may reduce IPC on load-heavy code, but they avoid extending the operand latch path with raw memory load-data forwarding.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` invokes `cosim-build` before the Python eval wrapper can inject `NRET=1`; the bare invocation therefore built the harness as NRET=2 and failed looking for `_1` RVFI ports. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matched `core.yaml`.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the EXA/EXB split in `cores/bench/rtl/` and wrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Formal: pass, `53 passed / 0 failed`\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, `2 ELFs tested`\n\nNote: bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` builds the harness as `NRET=2` before the eval wrapper injects `core.yaml`’s `nret: 1`, so it fails looking for `_1` RVFI ports."}}
