{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Decoupled two-entry instruction fetch queue\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced the old combinational IF/ID boundary in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with a two-entry PC/instruction FIFO.\n- Added an empty-queue bypass path so zero-wait imem still feeds decode in the same cycle, avoiding an extra steady-state fetch bubble.\n- Fetch advances on `io_imemReady` when the queue has space, or when decode pops an entry in the same cycle. Backend stalls no longer stop sequential fetch unless the two-entry queue is full.\n- Redirects flush both FIFO entries and restart fetch at the EX redirect target.\n- Reworked `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` to output an IF pop/decode-accept handshake. Imem stalls now bubble decode only when the front end has no queued or bypassed instruction.\n- Updated `rtl/core.sv` wiring for the new IF queue handshake.\n\nDeviations:\n- Did not add new metadata types in `core_pkg.sv`; the existing `if_id_t` is sufficient for the queued payload.\n- Kept ID stage unchanged. Its existing hold/bubble controls already match the required \"capture only when decode accepts\" behavior once the queue pop is controlled by the hazard unit.\n\nConcerns:\n- The queue is intentionally only two entries. It can hide short imem stalls after backend-created slack, but longer imem gaps still drain it.\n- When the queue is full and decode does not pop, a ready imem response is ignored and the same fetch PC is retried later. This matches the no-valid imem interface available to this core.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv` passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed: 53 passed, 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` without `NRET=1` failed in the harness build because it compiled `main.cpp` with `-DNRET=2` while `core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed: `{\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the two-entry decoupled instruction fetch queue in `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv`, with pop-based hazard control in `hazard_unit.sv` and updated top-level wiring in `core.sv`. Redirects flush the queue, and empty-queue bypass preserves zero-wait throughput.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: passed\n- Formal: passed, `53 passed, 0 failed`\n- Cosim: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed, 2 ELFs tested\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` has a local harness mismatch here because it defaults to `NRET=2` despite `core.yaml` declaring `nret: 1`\n\nWrote notes to `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`. Timing was not run."}}
