{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_66", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/rtl/store_buffer.sv && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/store_buffer.sv\n//\n// One-entry write buffer for ordinary RAM stores.  When MEM sees a RAM store\n// and the external dmem bus is not ready, the store retires architecturally\n// and this buffer keeps retrying the physical write until io_dmemReady.\n//\n// Latency:        enqueue at MEM/WB retirement, retry until ready.\n// RVFI fields:    none directly; MEM/WB keeps reporting the retired store.\nmodule store_buffer (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n\n  input  logic        enqueue,\n  input  logic [31:0] enqueue_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0] enqueue_wdata,\n  input  logic [3:0]  enqueue_wmask,\n\n  input  logic        dmem_ready,\n\n  output logic        busy,\n  output logic [31:0] dmem_addr,\n  output logic [31:0] dmem_wdata,\n  output logic [3:0]  dmem_wen\n);\n\n  logic        valid_q;\n  logic [31:0] addr_q;\n  logic [31:0] wdata_q;\n  logic [3:0]  wmask_q;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      valid_q <= 1'b0;\n      addr_q  <= 32'b0;\n      wdata_q <= 32'b0;\n      wmask_q <= 4'b0000;\n    end else if (enqueue) begin\n      valid_q <= 1'b1;\n      addr_q  <= enqueue_addr;\n      wdata_q <= enqueue_wdata;\n      wmask_q <= enqueue_wmask;\n    end else if (valid_q && dmem_ready) begin\n      valid_q <= 1'b0;\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign busy       = valid_q;\n  assign dmem_addr  = addr_q;\n  assign dmem_wdata = wdata_q;\n  assign dmem_wen   = valid_q ? wmask_q : 4'b0000;\n\nendmodule\n## One-entry nonblocking store buffer\n\n### What changed\n\n- Added `rtl/store_buffer.sv`, a one-entry RAM-store retry buffer. It latches\n  aligned address, replicated write data, and byte mask when MEM sees a normal\n  RAM store while `io_dmemReady` is low.\n- Updated `rtl/mem_stage.sv` to distinguish blocking memory cases from\n  bufferable stores:\n  - loads still block until dmem is ready;\n  - MMIO, marker, and OOB stores remain blocking and are never buffered;\n  - normal RAM stores enqueue and retire when dmem is stalled and the buffer is\n    empty;\n  - younger memory ops block while the pending buffered write owns the port.\n- Updated `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` to consume a MEM-stage `mem_block` signal rather\n  than rebuilding a simple `!dmem_ready && ex_mem_mem_op` stall.\n- Updated `rtl/core.sv` to instantiate the store buffer and mux the external\n  dmem outputs between the MEM-stage request and the pending buffered write.\n- Added `store_buffer.sv` to the cocotb pipeline test source list.\n\n### Deviations\n\n- The buffer is integrated as a top-level dmem-output mux rather than hidden\n  fully inside `mem_stage`, so the structural ownership of the external dmem\n  port is explicit in `core.sv`.\n- Buffered writes drive an aligned dmem address. Direct MEM-stage stores keep\n  the existing effective-address output behavior.\n\n### Concerns\n\n- Younger non-memory instructions can retire while a RAM store is pending in\n  the buffer, as intended. A later memory operation, including MMIO timing\n  markers, stalls behind the pending write.\n- The repository `make cosim TARGET=bench` path invokes `cosim-build` before\n  the Python cosim driver injects `NRET` from `core.yaml`; plain make therefore\n  tried to compile the nret=1 core with `-DNRET=2`. Running the same target with\n  `NRET=1` exercises the intended single-retire cosim path.\n\n### Local status\n\n- Lint: pass\n  `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- Formal: pass\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n  Result: 53 passed, 0 failed.\n- Cosim: pass with nret override\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n  Result: `{\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}`.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench`: did not reach RTL simulation because the\n  first Verilator build used `-DNRET=2` against this nret=1 core.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
