{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Static BTFN fetch predictor implementation notes\n\nChanged:\n- Added `pred_next_pc` to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\n- Added IF-side static prediction for backward conditional branches and JAL.\n- Changed EX redirect generation to compare the architectural next PC against the predicted next PC, while keeping RVFI `pc_wdata` equal to the resolved architectural next PC.\n- Added guarded `core_pkg.sv` includes to RTL modules that depend on shared typedefs/constants so the required wildcard Verilator lint command is source-order safe.\n\nDeviations:\n- IF only predicts branch/JAL targets whose computed target is word-aligned. Misaligned control transfers are trap-class in this core and stay sequential so EX can retire them with `pc+4`.\n- IF checks branch `funct3` validity before predicting a branch opcode, avoiding speculation on reserved branch encodings.\n\nConcerns:\n- The IF-stage predictor adds immediate decode and a selected target adder on the fetch PC path, so timing should be checked by the vendor flow.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout invoked the harness with default `NRET=2` and failed to compile against this `nret: 1` core; `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
