{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '98,132p' cores/bench/rtl/core.sv && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"  logic        wb_w_en;\n  logic [4:0]  wb_w_addr;\n  logic [31:0] wb_w_data;\n\n  // ── IF ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  if_stage u_if (\n    .clock           (clock),\n    .reset           (reset),\n    .stall           (stall_if),\n    .flush           (flush_if),\n    .redirect        (redirect),\n    .redirect_target (redirect_target),\n    .pred_redirect   (pred_redirect),\n    .pred_redirect_target (pred_redirect_target),\n    .imem_addr       (io_imemAddr),\n    .imem_data       (io_imemData),\n    .out             (if_id_w)\n  );\n\n  // ── ID + regfile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  id_stage u_id (\n    .clock    (clock),\n    .reset    (reset),\n    .hold     (hold_id),\n    .bubble   (bubble_id),\n    .in       (if_id_w),\n    .rs1_addr (rs1_addr_w),\n    .rs2_addr (rs2_addr_w),\n    .rs1_data (rs1_data_w),\n    .rs2_data (rs2_data_w),\n    .pred_redirect        (pred_redirect),\n    .pred_redirect_target (pred_redirect_target),\n    .out      (id_ex_w)\n  );\n\nDecode-side static branch predictor\n===================================\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added `pred_next_pc` to the ID/EX bundle.\n- Added decode-side static prediction for aligned direct control flow:\n  backward conditional branches predict taken, forward conditional branches\n  predict fall-through, and direct JAL predicts taken. JALR remains unresolved\n  until EX.\n- IF now accepts a decode prediction redirect alongside the existing EX\n  correction redirect. The decode redirect updates the next PC without\n  invalidating the current IF/ID payload, because this core has no registered\n  IF/ID stage and the current payload is the branch/JAL making the prediction.\n- EX computes the architectural next PC and redirects only when it differs\n  from the carried predicted next PC.\n\nDeviations:\n- I did not add a functional hazard_unit dependency for decode redirects.\n  In this pipeline shape, the ID stage already receives `hold` and `bubble`,\n  so it suppresses early redirects whenever the decoded instruction will not\n  actually enter ID/EX. Feeding the decode redirect back into `flush_if` would\n  incorrectly kill the branch/JAL itself.\n- Misaligned direct targets are not predicted in ID. They keep the existing\n  linear trap behavior and resolve as pc+4 in EX.\n\nConcerns:\n- The decode target adder now sits in ID, not IF. It should stay off the fetch\n  PC recurrence, but it is still new ID-stage work.\n- Local `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults the harness to `NRET=2` and fails\n  to build this `nret: 1` core. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches the declared\n  core contract and passes.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n  `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
