{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Single-entry last-target predictor implementation notes\n\n- Added IF/ID and ID/EX prediction metadata: `pred_valid` plus `pred_pc`.\n- Added a one-entry exact-PC predictor in `if_stage.sv` with one valid bit,\n  one PC tag, and one resolved target. On a hit, fetch uses the stored target\n  as the next PC and carries the predicted next PC with the instruction.\n- Added EX-side prediction resolution in `ex_stage.sv`. A miss is treated as\n  an implicit `pc+4` prediction; EX redirects only when the resolved next PC\n  differs from the carried/default prediction.\n- Trained the entry only from valid, legal, aligned taken conditional branches\n  and direct JALs. JALR is not trained. A valid, legal not-taken conditional\n  branch asks IF to invalidate the entry only if the stored tag matches that\n  branch PC.\n- Kept stale predictor hits on non-control instructions correct by comparing\n  every valid instruction's resolved architectural next PC against the carried\n  prediction. This is mostly for formal robustness under arbitrary instruction\n  streams; normal static code should only hit entries trained at branch/JAL PCs.\n\nDeviations / concerns\n\n- I did not add fetch-time immediate decode, target adders, counters, or a\n  multi-entry table.\n- I did not carry the prediction metadata into EX/MEM because EX consumes it\n  before the EX/MEM register. The RVFI-facing `pc_next` continues to use the\n  resolved architectural next PC.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults the C++ harness to `NRET=2` in this\n  checkout, which fails to build against the declared `nret: 1` port set before\n  simulation. Re-running as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matches\n  `core.yaml` and passed.\n\nLocal status\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed, run as\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELFs tested, run as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
