{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Queued-entry static branch predictor\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added `pred_valid` and `pred_next_pc` metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\n- Extended the two-entry IF FIFO with per-entry prediction metadata. Predictions are generated only for instructions that are stored in the FIFO, never for the empty-FIFO bypass path.\n- IF predecodes FIFO pushes for legal-looking backward conditional branches and direct JALs, records the computed target only when it is word-aligned, and redirects fetch to the registered target when a predicted FIFO head is popped by decode.\n- ID latches the prediction metadata with the decoded instruction and clears `pred_valid` on bubbles.\n- EX computes the resolved architectural next PC, suppresses redirects for correct queued predictions, and redirects to the resolved next PC on prediction misses. Unpredicted taken branches and jumps keep the previous redirect behavior.\n\nDeviations:\n- Reserved branch funct3 values are not predicted, even if their B-immediate is backward, so illegal branch encodings keep the existing trap/linear-PC behavior.\n- JALR/returns remain unpredicted as planned.\n\nConcerns:\n- The FIFO push path now has B/J immediate target adders feeding queue metadata registers. This avoids the active empty-bypass PC recurrence, but it may still add some fetch-PC fanout and IF register input timing.\n- Correctness depends on the queue-head prediction redirect happening only on `decode_pop`; load-use, dmem, mul/div busy, and EX redirects all suppress the pop through the existing hazard path.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: local invocation failed before RTL simulation because the harness defaulted to `NRET=2` and looked for channel-1 ports on this `nret: 1` core.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, selftest and CoreMark both tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the queued-entry static branch predictor in `cores/bench/rtl/`.\n\nChanged:\n- Added prediction metadata through IF/ID and ID/EX.\n- Stored static predictions only on IF FIFO pushes.\n- Redirected IF on predicted FIFO-head pop.\n- Suppressed EX redirect on correct predictions and repaired misses to the resolved next PC.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, `53 passed / 0 failed`.\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nWrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md` with the details."}}
