{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r9s0\\\") | \\\"TITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nMOTIVATION:\\\\n\\\\(.motivation)\\\\nHYP:\\\\n\\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis)\\\\nCHANGES:\\\\n\\\\(.changes)\\\\nCRIT: \\\\(.critical_path.from) -> \\\\(.critical_path.to), cells=\\\\(.critical_path.logic_cells), fmax=\\\\(.fmax_mhz)\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"TITLE: Lazy IF FIFO payload invalidation\nMOTIVATION:\nThe current winner's worst paths repeatedly involve the regfile/EX redirect\ncone reaching into the two-entry IF queue, especially count and payload\nupdate flops. Prior attempts that added prediction or rewrote the FIFO\ncontrol regressed, but the successful ID/EX bubble split showed that this\ncore benefits when wide payload registers are decoupled from narrow validity\ncontrol.\n\nHYP:\nKeep the existing two-entry IF FIFO and its count-based policy, but stop\nclearing or rewriting the queued pc/instruction payload on reset, redirect,\nand pop-to-empty cases. Only fetch_pc and count_q need architecturally\nmeaningful reset/redirect behavior; when count_q is zero, pc0/pc1/instr0/\ninstr1 are unobservable, and when count_q invalidates an entry the stale\nbits cannot reach decode or RVFI.\n\nThis should delete high-fanout redirect/reset muxing from roughly 128 bits\nof IF queue payload while preserving the exact queue occupancy, bypass, and\ndecode-pop semantics. The expected IPC is unchanged, so any gain comes from\nFmax by reducing the fragile EX-redirect-to-IF update cone without adding\npredictor state, target adders, or memory-side muxing.\n\nCHANGES:\n[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Invalidate the IF FIFO by count only: reset and redirect clear count/fetch PC but leave stale queued pc/instruction payload bits untouched, and pop-to-empty no longer writes zero payloads.\"}]\nCRIT: cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 -> cpu/u_if/pc0_q_4_s0, cells=30, fmax=64.589\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
