{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r6s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\\\") | \\\"ID \\\\(.id) \\\\(.title) outcome=\\\\(.outcome) delta=\\\\(.delta_pct) fmax=\\\\(.fmax_mhz)\\\\nHYP: \\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis)\\\\n---\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "ID hyp-20261003-001-r5s0 Slim IF redirect handshake outcome=regression delta=-3.99 fmax=61.731\nHYP: Refactor the IF queue so redirect remains only a top-priority sequential\nflush of fetch_pc and FIFO contents, while the normal bypass/out_valid,\ndecode-pop, and imem-push equations are computed without redirect in their\ncombinational cones. The hazard unit already suppresses decode_pop and\nbubbles ID/EX on redirect, and the IF always_ff block already ignores normal\nqueue activity when redirect is asserted, so the extra redirect terms in\nbypass_valid, out_valid, do_pop, and do_push are redundant. Removing them\nshould shorten the current EX-redirect-to-IF-count timing path without adding\nbranch penalty, predictor state, or any new pipeline bubbles.\n\n---\nID hyp-20261003-001-r6s0 Clear-coded IF FIFO flush outcome=regression delta=-4.66 fmax=61.295\nHYP: Recode the two-entry IF queue around per-entry valid bits, or an equivalent\nclear-friendly representation, and split the fetch PC update from the FIFO\nvalidity update. On EX redirect, invalidate only the tiny queue valid/count\nstate and load fetch_pc_q with the redirect target; the queued pc/instruction\npayload flops can be left unchanged because invalid entries are never\npresented to decode. Reset can still initialize payloads for cleanliness.\nNormal push, pop, bypass, and sequential PC+4 behavior stay unchanged.\n\nThis targets the reported u_id -> u_ex -> u_if worst path more directly\nthan the failed handshake slimming: redirect still flushes wrong-path queued\ninstructions in the same cycle, but it no longer fans out into wide payload\nclearing or a normal-data mux feeding the FIFO count/payload next-state\nlogic. Because the FIFO depth, predictor-free PC recurrence, and stall-hiding\nbehavior are unchanged, the expected gain is mostly Fmax with minimal IPC\nrisk.\n\n---\nID hyp-20261003-001-r10s0 Implicit-PC IF FIFO outcome=regression delta=-0.71 fmax=63.834\nHYP: The IF FIFO only ever holds sequential instructions between redirects, and a\nredirect already flushes the queue before fetching from the new target. That\nmeans queued PCs can be derived from fetch_pc_q and count_q instead of being\nstored and shifted as pc0_q/pc1_q payload. Replace the explicit queued-PC\nregisters with an implicit head-PC calculation: for count 1 the head PC is\nfetch_pc_q - 4, for count 2 it is fetch_pc_q - 8, and the empty bypass still\nuses fetch_pc_q directly.\n\nInstruction payload storage, count transitions, imem push, decode pop, and\nredirect flush semantics stay unchanged, so CoreMark's stall-hiding IPC\nshould match the champion. The expected win is Fmax: the redirect/decode-pop\nfeedback no longer drives wide queued-PC register muxes, and recent timing\nreports often name pc0_q or nearby IF payload state as the endpoint.\n\n---\nID hyp-20261003-001-r11s0 Shared EX target adder outcome=regression delta=4.18 fmax=66.981\nHYP: Refactor ex_stage so PC-relative branch and JAL targets share one target\ncomputation instead of building separate full-width branch_target and\njump_target adders. Because the core fetches aligned RV32I instructions and\nB/J immediates have bit 0 fixed to zero, PC-relative target misalignment can\nbe detected from imm[1], and aligned redirect targets can be formed with a\n30-bit word-address add plus 2'b00. Keep the full rs1+imm adder only for\nJALR, whose bit 0 is architecturally cleared.\n\nAlso compute pc_plus4 once and reuse it for link writeback, fall-through\npc_next, and the held mul/div payload. This should remove duplicated\nadders and low-bit target checks from the EX-to-IF redirect cone while\nleaving IPC, RVFI pc_wdata, and misalignment trap behavior unchanged.\n\n---\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
