{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Isolate unused EX operand cones\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core is limited by short but fragile paths through decode,\n  forwarding, execute, and the IF FIFO redirect controls. Prior wins came from\n  removing common-cone work, while attempts that added predictor state,\n  metadata, or extra target plumbing usually regressed. In the current EX\n  stage, forwarded rs1/rs2 operands still feed the generic ALU, the load/store\n  address adder, and the JALR adder even on instruction classes that do not use\n  those results, increasing fanout near the redirect path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add explicit operand isolation in ex_stage so each forwarded operand only\n  drives the arithmetic cone needed by the decoded instruction class. For\n  conditional branches, keep the operands on the branch comparator but feed\n  neutral constants into the generic ALU and memory-address adder; for\n  load/store, drive only the dedicated rs1+imm memory-address adder and store\n  data path; for direct JAL, keep only the pc+4/link and pc+imm bookkeeping;\n  for JALR, keep the rs1+imm target adder but do not also exercise the generic\n  ALU/memory-address cone.\n\n  This should reduce forwarded-operand fanout and LUT packing pressure on the\n  recurring u_fwd/u_ex/u_if critical path without changing branch latency,\n  FIFO behavior, RVFI semantics, or CoreMark instruction count. The important\n  constraint is to avoid the failed \"bypass generic ALU for adds\" pattern:\n  do not add a second result mux for normal ALU instructions, only clamp\n  unused side cones for non-ALU instruction classes whose results are already\n  ignored downstream.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate the inputs of unused EX side cones by instruction class so branch/JAL/JALR/memory operations do not unnecessarily drive the generic ALU or unrelated address adders.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep memory-stage outputs and RVFI memory fields semantically identical while tolerating zeroed inactive mem_addr_fast values for non-memory operations.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for branch, JAL, JALR, load/store, and ALU dependencies to ensure operand isolation does not alter redirects, traps, writeback, or memory masks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
