{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r2s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Split ID/EX bubble control from payload data\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  After the RV32M split, the vendor timing path moved to a much smaller\n  regfile-to-ID/EX path that loops through execute redirect, fetch flush,\n  hazard control, and back into the ID/EX register enables. The data payload\n  bits of the ID/EX register do not need to be cleared on redirect, load-use,\n  or mul/div busy bubbles as long as the valid bit and side-effecting control\n  fields are bubbled. Removing those fast-changing bubble conditions from the\n  wide rs1/rs2/pc/instr/immediate payload muxes should shorten the new critical\n  cone without changing instruction retirement semantics.\nhypothesis: |\n  Refactor the ID stage so the ID/EX register has separate hold and bubble\n  behavior for side-effecting control versus payload data. On dmem stalls, the\n  whole ID/EX bundle must still hold because an older memory op is blocking the\n  pipeline. On load-use, redirect, imem bubble, and execute-busy cycles, only\n  ctrl/valid need to become a bubble; pc, rs values, immediates, register\n  numbers, and instr may capture the current fetch/regfile values because the\n  invalid zero-control instruction cannot redirect, access memory, or write\n  back. This removes redirect/load-use/ex_busy logic from the D path and enable\n  path of the wide ID/EX payload flops, targeting the current 41-cell\n  regfile-to-ID/EX worst path while keeping the same single-retire contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate the ID/EX hold condition needed for dmem stalls from bubble conditions caused by load-use hazards, redirects, and execute-busy cycles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split the ID/EX register update so payload fields only hold on true pipeline holds, while ctrl/valid are zeroed for bubbles.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the renamed hold/bubble intent between hazard control and decode without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
