{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r3s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Bypass ALU mux for memory addresses\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  After the RV32M split and the ID/EX bubble cleanup, the reported worst path\n  is a much smaller execute cone that still runs through u_ex/u_alu before\n  reaching memory-side timing endpoints. Loads and stores only need rs1+imm for\n  the data-memory address, but today that address is carried in the same\n  generic alu_result field used by shifts, compares, logical ops, AUIPC, and\n  jump link results. That makes every memory access pay for the full ALU result\n  selection even though the operation is always an add.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a dedicated fast memory-address path in EX and carry it separately into\n  MEM. The EX stage should compute mem_addr_fast = forwarded_rs1 + imm for\n  load/store instructions and register that value in EX/MEM beside the existing\n  alu_result. The MEM stage should use this dedicated address for dmem_addr,\n  byte-lane masks, misalignment checks, and RVFI aligned mem_addr construction,\n  while leaving alu_result for non-memory writeback behavior. This removes the\n  generic ALU case/output mux from the hot dmem address path without changing\n  pipeline depth, bus handshakes, RVFI retirement, or CoreMark-visible memory\n  semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated memory effective-address field to the EX/MEM bundle so memory address timing no longer depends on the generic ALU result field.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute and register a fast rs1+imm address for loads and stores in parallel with the existing ALU, preserving forwarding and trap behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive dmem_addr, byte masks, misalignment detection, and RVFI aligned memory address fields from the dedicated memory-address field.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
