{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Clear-coded IF FIFO flush\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's timing path still runs from decoded/executing branch\n  state into the two-entry IF FIFO count or payload registers. The previous\n  slim-handshake attempt showed that merely deleting redundant redirect terms\n  from local push/pop equations does not remove the real redirect-to-FIFO-state\n  arc. The next smallest lever is to preserve the useful two-entry queue while\n  changing how its flush state is represented and mapped.\nhypothesis: |\n  Recode the two-entry IF queue around per-entry valid bits, or an equivalent\n  clear-friendly representation, and split the fetch PC update from the FIFO\n  contents/count update. On reset or EX redirect, the queue valid/count and\n  queued payload registers should be cleared through a top-priority synchronous\n  clear style, while fetch_pc_q alone loads the redirect target. Normal push,\n  pop, bypass, and sequential PC+4 behavior stay unchanged.\n\n  This targets the reported u_id -> u_ex -> u_if worst path more directly\n  than the failed handshake slimming: redirect still flushes wrong-path queued\n  instructions in the same cycle, but it no longer has to be implemented as a\n  wide normal-data mux feeding the FIFO count/payload next-state logic. Because\n  the FIFO depth, predictor-free PC recurrence, and stall-hiding behavior are\n  unchanged, the expected gain is mostly Fmax with minimal IPC risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recode the two-entry IF FIFO state with clear-friendly valid/count handling, separating redirect flush of queue contents from redirect loading of fetch_pc_q while preserving the existing decode_pop interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
