{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r7s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Late store-data forwarding\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is no longer dominated by arithmetic; recent attempts\n  that touched the IF redirect loop or added prediction mostly lost Fmax.\n  One remaining low-risk CoreMark inefficiency is the conservative load-use\n  interlock: every instruction after a load stalls when either encoded source\n  field matches the load destination, even when rs2 is only store data that is\n  not needed until the following MEM stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the load-use hazard logic operand-role aware and add a late store-data\n  bypass into MEM. A store immediately after a load still must stall if the\n  loaded register is the store base address, because the address is needed in\n  EX, but it does not need to stall when the loaded register is only the store\n  data operand. In that case the store can enter EX with its old rs2 payload\n  and the MEM stage can replace the replicated write data with the load's\n  WB-stage value one cycle later. The same source-use predecode should also\n  avoid false load-use bubbles for I/U/J/fence/system encodings whose rs2 or\n  rs1 bitfields are immediates or destinations rather than real sources.\n\n  This targets iterations per cycle without adding target adders, predictors,\n  or new EX-to-IF feedback. The added compare and mux live on the store-data\n  side of MEM, while the current worst path is the branch/redirect-to-IF-count\n  control path, so the expected Fmax cost should be small.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Predecode whether the queued instruction actually uses rs1 and rs2 in EX, and suppress the load-use bubble for load-to-store-data cases while keeping load-to-store-base and ALU/branch hazards stalled.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a WB-to-store-data forwarding input path so a store in MEM can use the immediately preceding load result for dmem_wdata, RVFI mem_wdata, and the retired rs2 value.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the WB-stage destination/data metadata into MEM and pass enough IF/ID instruction information into hazard control for source-role-aware interlock decisions.\"\n  - file: test/test_load_store_forward.py\n    description: \"Add a focused cocotb test for load followed by store-data dependency, plus guard cases that still require a stall when the loaded value is the store address or an ALU/branch operand.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
