{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261003-.*r[0-9]+s[0-9].*(structural|EX|MEM|IF FIFO|muldiv|pipeline|stage|retim|sidecar|buffer|split)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Register early forwarding selects\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move forwarding hit detection one stage earlier and latch the selected\\nbypass source with the ID/EX payload. For an instruction being decoded,\\ncompare its rs1/rs2 against the producer currently in ID/EX, which will be\\nEX/MEM when the consumer executes, and against the producer currently in\\nEX/MEM, which will be MEM/WB when the consumer executes. The EX stage then\\nuses registered forwarding selects, removing the rd comparator and priority\\nchain from the forwarding-to-ALU critical path. Load-use bubbling and dmem\\nstalls keep the same semantics by holding or clearing the latched selects\\nwith the rest of ID/EX.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add forwarding-select fields to the ID/EX bundle so bypass decisions are registered with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute next-cycle forwarding selects during decode from current pipeline destination metadata and latch them on ID/EX capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"desc\n…[176705 of 179777 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:caecfbfae4fa06d2]…\n4, \"delta_pct\": -15.59, \"vs_baseline\": 974.59, \"fmax_mhz\": 57.831, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4440325, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3131, \"ff\": 953, \"seeds\": [57.009, 57.831, 57.831], \"perturbations\": [[0, 57.009, 15], [1, 57.831, 15], [2, 57.831, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/instr0_q_2_s2\", \"slack_ns\": -12.541, \"arrival_ns\": 22.835, \"logic_cells\": 36, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T15:25:39.147190Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r13s2 (regression, -15.59%): Replacing metadata-free direct-JAL decode targets with a one-entry EX-trained exact cache regresses because `pc`/`instr` compares, cached-target muxing, and the ID/EX hit marker reintroduce predictor metadata while first-time JALs fall back to the slower EX redirect.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
