{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r14s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Parallel branch compare matrix\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path still runs from register/forwarding state through EX branch resolution into the IF FIFO redirect/flush update. Prior structural and predictor attempts show that adding fetch metadata, target caches, extra redirect registers, or delayed branch sidecars tends to lose either Fmax or CoreMark IPC. A narrower structural target is the branch comparator topology itself: conditional branches currently use the same post-forward 32-bit operand muxes as the ALU, so forwarding select logic sits in front of the branch compare and redirect decision.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure EX branch resolution as a small parallel compare matrix. For conditional branches, compute compare results for the possible rs1/rs2 forwarding sources in parallel, then use the existing forwarding selects only to choose the one-bit branch result. The ordinary ALU operand muxes remain for arithmetic, load/store address, JALR target, and RVFI operand reporting, but the timing-critical branch-taken-to-IF redirect path no longer needs to traverse two wide 3-way operand muxes before the equality or magnitude comparator.\n\n  This keeps the current metadata-free direct-JAL decode redirect, the two-entry IF FIFO, the single-cycle conditional branch resolution point, and all RVFI ordering semantics. It spends LUTs on duplicated branch compare logic rather than adding pipeline latency or front-end prediction state, aiming for a pure Fmax gain on the current u_id/u_ex/u_if critical cone with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refactor conditional branch resolution into a parallel forwarded-source compare matrix and select the final one-bit branch condition after forwarding selection, while leaving the existing ALU operand muxes and redirect timing intact.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_compare_matrix.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU with no forwarding, EX/MEM forwarding, MEM/WB forwarding, mixed-source forwarding, taken and untaken outcomes, and misaligned taken-target traps.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
