{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'muldiv|MUL|DIV|REM|RV32M|ex_busy|busy|done cycle|release|result-return|MD_DONE|CoreMark.*M|instruction mix|retired' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md cores/bench/implementation_notes.md 2>/dev/null\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/LESSONS.md:2:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r1s1 (improvement, +752.39%): Moving RV32M into a held multi-cycle EX unit is a large win when it removes multiply/divide/remainder hardware from the common ALU-forwarding-branch-address cone, because CoreMark's infrequent M ops tolerate stalls better than every integer op tolerates the long combinational path.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:4:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r2s0 (improvement, +24.85%): Splitting ID/EX bubbles so only valid/side-effecting control clears on redirect/load-use/imem/ex_busy cycles shortens the regfile-to-ID/EX cone because wide pc/rs/immediate/instr payload flops can capture freely while dmem stalls remain the only whole-bundle hold.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:5:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r2s1 (regression, +21.59%): Retiming redirect squash into EX can regress when the saved EX-to-hazard flush arc is replaced by high-fanout `squash_id_ex`/`execute_valid` gating across branch/jump, RV32M start, trap, and EX/MEM side-effect controls.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:11:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r4s1 (improvement, +5.76%): A two-entry IF FIFO helps CoreMark because load-use, dmem, and RV32M `ex_busy` holds let sequential fetch build slack that hides later `io_imemReady` gaps without adding predictor or target-adder delay to the PC loop.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:19:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r7s0 (regression, -1.34%): Operand-role-aware load-use stalls plus a WB-to-MEM store-data bypass regressed because CoreMark has too few load-to-store-data pairs to repay opcode predecode and MEM-stage compare/mux cost.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:22:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r8s0 (regression, -6.78%): Hoisting RV32M detection into a latched `ctrl_t.is_m_op` bit can cost more in ID/EX register width, decode fanout, and global control routing than the small EX `alu_op` M-op compare it replaces.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:23:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r8s1 (regression, -11.91%): Deferring conditional branches and JALR through an EX sidecar can lose because CoreMark p\n…[137212 of 140284 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cc3c1a4e629f3888]…\nession\", \"fitness\": 146.6, \"delta_pct\": -4.98, \"vs_baseline\": 1109.57, \"fmax_mhz\": 62.113, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4236938, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3009, \"ff\": 838, \"seeds\": [58.409, 62.113, 62.113], \"perturbations\": [[0, 58.409, 16], [1, 62.113, 17], [2, 62.113, 17]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/instr0_q_6_s2\", \"slack_ns\": -12.121, \"arrival_ns\": 22.415, \"logic_cells\": 40, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T15:41:58.490800Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r14s2 (regression, -4.98%): Even metadata-free backward-branch decode redirects regressed because `dec_is_branch && imm[31]` ID-to-IF redirect gating plus EX fallthrough-repair/taken-redirect muxing cost more than CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 2, "status": "failed"}}
