ready/done distinction local to ex_stage and the\n  hazard unit.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split the mul/div busy indication into wait-versus-result-emitting states so EX/MEM captures the completed M result while the front end is allowed to advance.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat the RV32M result-emitting cycle as ready unless a dmem stall is also holding EX/MEM, preserving load-use and redirect behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the refined execute-ready/execute-busy handshake between EX and hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_muldiv_release.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for MUL/DIV/REM followed by independent and dependent instructions, including dmem-stall overlap on the result cycle.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
