{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'regfile|reg_file|register file|LUTRAM|reset|store buffer|write buffer|branch target|predecode|decode queue|MEM/WB|WB' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/LESSONS.md:4:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r2s0 (improvement, +24.85%): Splitting ID/EX bubbles so only valid/side-effecting control clears on redirect/load-use/imem/ex_busy cycles shortens the regfile-to-ID/EX cone because wide pc/rs/immediate/instr payload flops can capture freely while dmem stalls remain the only whole-bundle hold.\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Register early forwarding selects\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move forwarding hit detection one stage earlier and latch the selected\\nbypass source with the ID/EX payload. For an instruction being decoded,\\ncompare its rs1/rs2 against the producer currently in ID/EX, which will be\\nEX/MEM when the consumer executes, and against the producer currently in\\nEX/MEM, which will be MEM/WB when the consumer executes. The EX stage then\\nuses registered forwarding selects, removing the rd comparator and priority\\nchain from the forwarding-to-ALU critical path. Load-use bubbling and dmem\\nstalls keep the same semantics by holding or clearing the latched selects\\nwith the rest of ID/EX.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"me\n…[39062 of 42134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1a3ec7b526fe99d8]…\nlta_pct\": -15.27, \"vs_baseline\": 908.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 54.299, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4441768, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3157, \"ff\": 882, \"seeds\": [55.043, 54.299, 54.299], \"perturbations\": [[0, 55.043, 17], [1, 54.299, 19], [2, 54.299, 19]], \"lutram\": 16, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc0_q_24_s2\", \"slack_ns\": -13.168, \"arrival_ns\": 23.462, \"logic_cells\": 36, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T12:55:07.182080Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r5s2 (regression, -15.27%): Even a 4-entry return-address stack that avoids front-end immediate decode can regress when canonical-JALR recognition and `ret_redirect`/`ret_pred_valid` repair plumbing create a new ID-to-IF/EX control path; CoreMark's return savings were too sparse to repay the timing cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
