{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r6s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Registered IF redirect aperture\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst vendor path still runs from register/ID state through EX branch or jump resolution into the IF FIFO count state. Prior predictor attempts lost because they added target lookup or immediate generation to the PC loop, and the earlier redirect-retiming attempt lost because it spread a new execute-side kill condition across side-effect controls. The remaining structural opportunity is to cut the EX-to-IF-queue state arc without adding prediction machinery or widening the EX side-effect cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny registered redirect aperture at the IF boundary. EX still resolves branches and jumps normally, and the same-cycle redirect may keep its existing narrow job of suppressing decode_pop and bubbling ID/EX so the immediately younger wrong-path instruction cannot enter execute. The structural change is that the IF FIFO count, entry valid bits, and fetch PC are no longer flushed or restarted directly from that same-cycle EX compare result. Instead, IF captures redirect plus target into a one-cycle pending redirect register and applies the queue flush/restart from that registered control on the following cycle. While the redirect is pending, hazard control continues to suppress decode_pop and bubble ID/EX so queued wrong-path instructions cannot advance; once the registered redirect is applied, normal two-entry sequential prefetch resumes.\n\n  This intentionally spends one extra recovery cycle on taken redirects, but it removes the current high-fanout combinational path into the IF queue state instead of adding predictor tags, target adders, or broad EX kill gating. If Gowin retimes the front end around local registered control, the Fmax gain should exceed the modest CoreMark IPC loss from the added taken-redirect cycle.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace direct EX redirect flushing of fetch_pc/count/entries with a registered pending-redirect latch that locally flushes and restarts the two-entry IF FIFO on the following cycle.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep same-cycle redirect as the narrow decode-pop suppressor/ID bubble source, and add a redirect-pending bubble source until the registered IF redirect has been applied, while preserving load-use, dmem, and ex_busy behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the IF redirect-pending/accepted handshake between EX, IF, and hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
