{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n \\\"category: structural|\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\"|structural|EX/MEM|MEM/WB|hazard|regfile|store|load|branch|FIFO|divider|muldiv\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Register early forwarding selects\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the critical path beginning at the MEM/WB\\ndestination register, passing through the forwarding unit, then through the\\nEX operand muxes and ALU before reaching the next state. That means a\\nsame-cycle forwarding comparison is controlling the ALU input path and\\ndirectly limiting Fmax, while contributing no useful IPC improvement beyond\\nordinary bypass correctness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move forwarding hit detection one stage earlier and latch the selected\\nbypass source with the ID/EX payload. For an instruction being decoded,\\ncompare its rs1/rs2 against the producer currently in ID/EX, which will be\\nEX/MEM when the consumer executes, and against the producer currently in\\nEX/MEM, which will be MEM/WB when the consumer executes. The EX stage then\\nuses registered forwarding selects, removing the rd comparator and priority\\nchain from the forwarding-to-ALU critical path. Load-use bubbling and dmem\\nstalls keep the same semantics by holding or clearing the latched selects\\nwith the rest of ID/EX.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add forwarding-select fields to the ID/EX bundle so bypass decisions are registered with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute next-cycle forwarding selects during decode from current pipeline destination metadata and latch them on ID/EX capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"de\n…[78607 of 81679 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a837d7753f535f57]…\ns_baseline\": 603.22, \"fmax_mhz\": 37.285, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4374632, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3385, \"ff\": 935, \"seeds\": [36.308, 37.285, 37.285], \"perturbations\": [[0, 36.308, 28], [1, 37.285, 29], [2, 37.285, 29]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_4_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pred_next0_q_4_s2\", \"slack_ns\": -22.542, \"arrival_ns\": 32.836, \"logic_cells\": 70, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 28, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T13:11:27.989662Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r6s2 (regression, -40.93%): Queued-only static prediction still regressed because FIFO push/dequeue now carries immediate predecode, target adders, `pred_pop` flush control, and EX `pred_next_pc` repair compares, so avoiding the empty-FIFO bypass path did not protect the IF/redirect timing point.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
