{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"One-entry nonblocking store buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's remaining successful changes avoid adding work to the\n  fragile fetch/redirect loop, but the pipeline still freezes on every dmem\n  stall for both loads and stores. With the evaluator injecting about 22% random\n  dmem backpressure, a store that has no destination register can unnecessarily\n  hold fetch, decode, execute, and retirement even when younger integer work\n  could safely proceed. CoreMark has enough stack and data stores that hiding\n  some store-side wait cycles should improve iterations per cycle without\n  touching the predictor-prone IF path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry store buffer at the MEM/dmem boundary for ordinary RAM stores.\n  When a store reaches MEM and dmem is not ready, latch its aligned address,\n  replicated write data, byte mask, and RVFI memory metadata into the buffer,\n  allow the store instruction to retire in order, and let younger non-memory\n  instructions continue while the buffer retries the external write. The buffer\n  owns the dmem port until the write is accepted; a younger load or store stalls\n  behind it, preserving memory ordering. MMIO and marker-range stores remain\n  blocking and are never buffered, so CoreMark timing brackets and UART behavior\n  stay exact.\n\n  This is a structural decoupling change rather than another front-end tweak:\n  loads still observe the existing ready/valid rule, RVFI order remains single\n  retire on channel 0, and the two-entry IF FIFO is left alone. The expected win\n  is IPC from overlapping random store wait cycles with later integer work, with\n  only a small Fmax cost from a local dmem-output mux and a memory-op stall\n  condition.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry RAM-only store buffer that latches pending store address/data/mask, retries the dmem write until io_dmemReady, and reports when the dmem port is occupied.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split store issue from load issue, enqueue stalled normal-RAM stores into the buffer, keep MMIO/marker stores blocking, and preserve RVFI memory fields for stores that retire after enqueue.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the simple dmem-ready stall with a MEM-stage block signal so the pipe stalls for loads, unbufferable stores, full-buffer stores, or younger memory ops behind a pending buffered write.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and wire the store buffer between MEM and the top-level dmem outputs while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
