{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r8s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Defer rs-dependent redirects\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best point is dominated by a short but fragile feedback cone from\n  regfile/read operands through EX branch or JALR resolution into the IF FIFO\n  redirect/flush controls. Prior predictors and store buffers lost because they\n  added new work to this boundary, while the successful structural changes won\n  by moving uncommon expensive work out of the normal single-cycle path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny held control-flow sidecar inside ex_stage for rs-dependent\n  redirects: conditional branches and JALR. When one of these instructions\n  enters EX, latch the forwarded operands and its RVFI payload, bubble EX/MEM\n  for one cycle, and assert the existing ex_busy backpressure so decode does\n  not accept a younger instruction. On the following cycle, resolve the branch\n  or JALR from the registered payload, emit the instruction to EX/MEM with the\n  correct pc_next, and drive redirect from the sidecar result. Direct JAL can\n  stay on the existing single-cycle path because it does not depend on rs data.\n\n  This should remove the regfile/forwarding-to-IF redirect clear path that has\n  repeatedly appeared in timing reports, without adding BTB tables, target\n  predecode, dmem ownership muxes, or an extra stage for ordinary ALU and memory\n  instructions. CoreMark will pay one extra cycle on conditional branches and\n  JALR, but the expected Fmax recovery should outweigh that smaller IPC loss.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-cycle registered control-flow sidecar for conditional branches and JALR, reusing the existing busy protocol and preserving direct JAL as a fast path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat the broadened ex_busy source as a generic held execute operation so IF/decode pause cleanly while the sidecar resolves.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Keep the existing ex_busy wiring and redirect interface intact while documenting that redirects for rs-dependent control flow are now registered.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_sidecar.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for taken/untaken conditional branches, JALR alignment behavior, and dependence on freshly forwarded operands through the sidecar.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
