{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Sidecar ordered branch compares\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path still runs from decoded operands through\n  EX branch resolution into the IF FIFO redirect/flush state. Prior attempts\n  that moved all rs-dependent control flow into a sidecar lost too much IPC,\n  but the full branch comparator still puts signed and unsigned less-than\n  hardware on the redirect cone even when hot loop branches are often simple\n  BEQ/BNE tests.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep equality branches, direct JAL, JALR, ALU ops, and memory ops on the\n  existing single-cycle EX path, but move ordered conditional branches\n  (BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU) into a tiny one-cycle execute sidecar. When an ordered\n  branch enters EX, latch the forwarded operands plus its PC, target, control,\n  and RVFI payload, bubble EX/MEM for one cycle through the existing ex_busy\n  backpressure, then resolve the less-than comparison from registered operands\n  on the following cycle and emit the original branch with the correct pc_next\n  and redirect.\n\n  This removes the signed/unsigned magnitude comparators and their branch-op\n  muxing from the normal EX-to-IF redirect path while preserving the common\n  BEQ/BNE loop branch latency that made the full control-flow sidecar regress.\n  CoreMark should pay an extra cycle only on the less frequent ordered branch\n  forms, while Fmax benefits from a narrower single-cycle redirect cone.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-cycle sidecar for BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU that latches forwarded operands and branch payload, reuses ex_busy, and keeps BEQ/BNE plus jumps on the existing fast path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Document and, if needed, slightly generalize the existing ex_busy interlock so ordered-branch sidecar cycles pause decode exactly like the current mul/div hold.\"\n  - file: test/test_ordered_branch_sidecar.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for taken and untaken signed/unsigned ordered branches, including forwarded operands and misaligned taken-target traps.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
