{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Metadata-free direct-JAL decode predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that this core cannot afford general fetch-time\n  prediction: BTBs, branch immediates, return stacks, loop counters, and\n  predicted-next-PC repair metadata repeatedly lengthened the IF redirect path.\n  The one predictor that nearly cleared the replacement threshold was the\n  narrow ID-stage direct-JAL redirect, because CoreMark benefits from removing\n  one redirect cycle on calls and direct jumps without predicting branch\n  direction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Revisit the direct-JAL-only predictor, but remove the carried \"already\n  redirected\" metadata that later variants added to the ID/EX bundle. When\n  decode actually accepts a valid, word-aligned JAL, compute pc plus the\n  existing J-immediate and send a decode-only redirect to the IF FIFO. This\n  redirect flushes younger queued sequential fetches but does not feed the\n  hazard unit's branch squash path, so the JAL itself still advances into EX.\n\n  In EX, suppress the normal redirect for aligned direct JALs by construction:\n  every valid aligned JAL reaching EX must have been accepted by decode and\n  therefore already redirected. Misaligned JAL targets still trap in EX, while\n  JALR and conditional branches keep the current EX-resolution behavior. This\n  keeps the profitable part of the near-miss direct-JAL predictor, avoids BTB\n  lookup and branch prediction state, and trims the extra pipeline metadata that\n  likely kept the previous result just below the tournament threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Emit a decode-only early redirect for accepted word-aligned direct JAL instructions using the existing decoded J-immediate path.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a separate decode-JAL redirect input that flushes younger queued entries and restarts fetch at the supplied target without triggering an ID/EX bubble.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress duplicate redirects for aligned direct JALs, while preserving architectural pc_next, link-register writeback, and misalignment trapping.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the decode-stage direct-JAL redirect to IF separately from the existing EX redirect and leave the nret=1 top-level interface unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_direct_jal_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for early direct-JAL redirection, duplicate-redirect suppression, and misaligned JAL fallback to the existing EX trap path.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
