{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Decode last-taken branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion finally found a predictor shape that pays: deterministic\n  direct-JAL redirects issued from decode with no predicted-next-PC metadata.\n  Earlier general predictors lost because they put immediate decode, target\n  adders, tag arrays, loop counters, or return-stack repair plumbing on the\n  fragile IF/redirect path. CoreMark still executes many hot conditional loop\n  backedges, so the remaining predictor opportunity is to predict only a branch\n  that has already been observed taken, while keeping the fetch stage almost as\n  simple as the champion.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor trained by EX when\n  a valid conditional branch resolves taken. Store the branch PC, the exact\n  instruction word, and the resolved target. In decode, when an accepted valid\n  branch matches both the stored PC and instruction word, redirect IF to the\n  stored target and latch only a one-bit predicted-taken marker into ID/EX.\n\n  EX still computes the real branch condition and target. If the marked branch\n  is taken, EX suppresses the duplicate redirect; if it falls through, EX\n  redirects to pc+4 to repair the loop exit. Matching the full instruction word\n  avoids carrying a 32-bit predicted target through the pipe for correctness\n  under symbolic instruction streams, while training from EX avoids any\n  fetch-time immediate decode or BTB lookup. This should recover repeated hot\n  loop-back redirect bubbles with much less timing cost than the failed IF BTB,\n  BTFN, countdown-loop, or RAS predictors.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted-taken branch marker to the ID/EX payload, without carrying a full predicted next PC or target.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Match accepted conditional branches against the single-entry PC/instruction predictor and emit a decode-stage predicted branch redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Generalize the existing decode redirect input so direct JAL and predicted branch redirects both flush younger queued sequential fetches without bubbling the accepted instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the predictor from resolved taken conditional branches and use the predicted-taken marker to suppress correct duplicate redirects or repair loop exits to pc+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the branch predictor training and decode redirect signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for repeated taken prediction, fall-through repair, exact-instruction mismatch, and unchanged behavior for unpredicted branches.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
