{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r13s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"EX-trained direct-JAL target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that the bench core cannot afford broad\n  front-end prediction: BTBs, BTFN decode, return stacks, loop counters, and\n  conditional-branch metadata have repeatedly lengthened the fragile IF/ID/EX\n  redirect cone. The current champion's useful predictor is much narrower:\n  decode redirects only accepted aligned direct JALs and carries no repair\n  metadata. Its remaining cost is that every direct JAL still computes a\n  decode-stage pc-plus-J-immediate target on the path into the IF FIFO.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the always-compute direct-JAL decode redirect with a tiny exact\n  direct-JAL target cache trained from EX. When EX resolves an aligned direct\n  JAL, store its pc, full instruction word, and resolved target. Decode then\n  early-redirects only when the accepted instruction is a direct JAL that\n  exactly matches the cached pc/instruction, using the stored target rather\n  than recomputing pc plus the J-immediate in ID. Cache misses simply fall\n  back to the normal EX redirect and train the cache for the next execution.\n\n  A one-bit ID/EX marker lets EX suppress the duplicate redirect only for\n  cache-hit JALs; unpredicted direct JALs still redirect in EX, while\n  misaligned JALs still trap and are not cached. This keeps the successful\n  predictor surface focused on repeated CoreMark call/jump sites, removes the\n  direct-JAL target adder from the decode-to-IF fast path, and avoids the\n  branch-direction state and predicted-next-PC metadata that hurt prior\n  predictor variants.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit ID/EX flag recording that this direct JAL was redirected from the exact target cache.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the unconditional direct-JAL target add with an exact pc/instruction target-cache lookup and cache-hit decode redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the direct-JAL cache from resolved aligned direct JALs and suppress duplicate EX redirects only for marked cache hits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire EX-side direct-JAL cache training back to decode while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_jal_target_cache.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for cache-hit early redirects, cache-miss EX fallback, exact-instruction mismatch, and misaligned JAL non-caching.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
