{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Metadata-free backward branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that the front end cannot afford tables,\n  tags, loop counters, return stacks, or carried predicted-next-PC metadata.\n  The current champion succeeds only for aligned direct JAL because decode\n  redirects with no repair metadata and EX can suppress the duplicate redirect\n  deterministically. CoreMark still contains hot backward conditional branches,\n  and the existing decode stage already computes pc+imm for the direct-JAL\n  redirect path, so there is a narrow opportunity to predict loop backedges\n  without adding another target adder or predictor state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the current metadata-free decode redirect from aligned direct JAL to\n  aligned negative-offset conditional branches using a static backward-taken,\n  forward-not-taken policy. In ID, when an accepted valid conditional branch\n  has a negative B-immediate and the existing pc+imm target is word-aligned,\n  redirect the IF queue to that target just like the current direct-JAL path.\n\n  Do not add a BTB, tag compare, counter, target cache, or predicted-next-PC\n  field. EX can recompute the same static policy from the carried branch\n  immediate and resolved target: suppress the duplicate redirect when the\n  backward branch is actually taken, repair to pc+4 when the predicted\n  backward branch falls through, and keep the current taken redirect for\n  forward branches. This should harvest CoreMark loop-back IPC while avoiding\n  the specific metadata and compare costs that sank the last-taken branch\n  predictor.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Generalize the existing accepted-instruction decode redirect so aligned negative-offset conditional branches reuse the current pc+imm target path alongside direct JAL.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recompute the static backward-taken policy from the ID/EX branch immediate, suppress correct duplicate taken redirects, and repair predicted-taken loop exits to pc+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Rename or generalize the decode redirect input so both direct JAL and static backward-branch redirects flush queued sequential fetches without bubbling the accepted instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the generalized decode redirect signals between ID and IF while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_static_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for predicted backward taken branches, loop-exit repair, forward taken branches, misaligned target suppression, and unchanged direct-JAL behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
