{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r15s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Compressed direct-JAL decode predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that this core cannot afford front-end tables,\n  tags, return stacks, loop counters, or carried prediction metadata. The only\n  predictor-like change that improved the champion is the current metadata-free\n  aligned direct-JAL decode redirect, but its target calculation still uses the\n  full 32-bit immediate generator and byte-address adder on the accepted-JAL\n  ID-to-IF flush path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing predictor surface exactly as narrow as the champion's:\n  accepted, legal, aligned direct JAL only. Recode that path as a word-PC\n  target predictor that recognizes opcode 1101111 directly from the IF/ID\n  instruction, forms only the J-immediate bits [31:2], and adds them to\n  in.pc[31:2]. The decode redirect target is then {word_target, 2'b00}; no\n  BTB, tag, counter, branch prediction, return stack, or predicted-next-PC\n  metadata is added.\n\n  This should preserve the CoreMark IPC win from early direct-JAL redirects\n  while shortening the current decode-to-IF target/flush cone by avoiding the\n  generic imm_gen output, low-bit alignment check, and full byte-address adder\n  on the predictor path. EX still computes architectural pc_next, traps\n  misaligned JAL/JALR targets, and suppresses the duplicate aligned-JAL\n  redirect exactly as today.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the direct-JAL predictor target path with a narrow opcode-specific word-PC J-immediate adder and an alignment-by-construction redirect target.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep architectural jump target, misalignment trap, RVFI pc_next, and aligned direct-JAL duplicate-redirect suppression semantics unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the existing metadata-free decode redirect interface and FIFO flush behavior while accepting the word-aligned direct-JAL target.\"\n  - file: test/test_direct_jal_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for aligned direct-JAL early redirects, negative and positive J-immediates, link writeback, and unchanged JALR/misaligned-trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
