{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Static BTFN fetch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current pipeline fetches sequentially and resolves every taken branch or\n  jump in EX, forcing wrong-path instructions to be flushed. CoreMark contains\n  tight loops and frequent unconditional JAL control flow, so the always-not-\n  taken policy pays the redirect penalty repeatedly on hot backward branches\n  and calls even when their targets are immediate constants available at fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small static predictor in IF that decodes only enough of io_imemData to\n  recognize conditional branches with negative B-immediates and unconditional\n  JAL instructions. Fetch should set the next PC to the predicted target for\n  backward branches and all JALs, carry the predicted next PC through ID/EX, and\n  let EX redirect only when the actual next PC differs from the prediction.\n  Correctly predicted loop backedges and JALs then avoid the two younger\n  wrong-path bubbles, while forward branches and JALR keep the existing\n  correction behavior. The added IF decode/adder is small compared with the\n  current ALU/forwarding critical path, so the expected gain is primarily IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so EX can distinguish correct predictions from mispredicts.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Decode branch/JAL immediates in fetch and choose the predicted next PC using a backward-taken, forward-not-taken static policy plus always-taken JAL.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted next PC alongside the decoded instruction while preserving existing stall and flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the actual next PC and assert redirect only on a prediction mismatch or unresolved JALR target, while keeping RVFI pc_wdata equal to the architectural next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predictor metadata through the pipeline and keep redirect flushes tied to EX mispredicts.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
