{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Decode-side static branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing core still pays an EX-stage redirect penalty for every taken\n  direct branch and JAL. Prior predictor attempts lost because they placed\n  immediate decode, target addition, tag lookup, and target muxing directly on\n  the fetch PC loop. CoreMark's hot loops are still attractive, but the next\n  predictor needs to stay off the IF critical path as much as possible.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-side static predictor for direct control flow: predict backward\n  conditional branches taken, forward conditional branches not taken, and JAL\n  always taken. The IF stage continues to fetch pc+4 by default, while ID\n  computes the branch/JAL target from the already-decoded instruction and sends\n  an early redirect for predicted-taken direct control transfers. Carry the\n  predicted next PC into EX so the existing branch/jump resolver only redirects\n  on a prediction mismatch or unresolved JALR. This should recover one cycle on\n  hot loop backedges and direct jumps without adding a BTB lookup, counter RAM,\n  or instruction-immediate adder to the fetch-stage PC recurrence.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the ID/EX bundle so EX can compare the decode prediction against the resolved architectural next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize direct branches and JAL in decode, compute the static predicted next PC, and emit an early redirect for predicted-taken direct control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the carried predicted next PC to suppress redirects on correct predictions and redirect only when the actual branch or jump next PC differs.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept an early decode redirect alongside the existing EX redirect while keeping the normal fetch path as pc+4 on predictor misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat decode-predicted redirects as a front-end bubble source without changing dmem stalls, imem stalls, load-use hazards, or execute-busy behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the decode prediction metadata and early redirect signals between ID, IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the nret=1 IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
