{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"hyp-20261003-001-r3s0|136.43|predictor|BTB|BTFN\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static BTFN fetch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline fetches sequentially and resolves every taken branch or\\njump in EX, forcing wrong-path instructions to be flushed. CoreMark contains\\ntight loops and frequent unconditional JAL control flow, so the always-not-\\ntaken policy pays the redirect penalty repeatedly on hot backward branches\\nand calls even when their targets are immediate constants available at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline fetches sequentially and resolves every taken branch or\\njump in EX, forcing wrong-path instructions to be flushed. CoreMark contains\\ntight loops and frequent unconditional JAL control flow, so the always-not-\\ntaken policy pays the redirect penalty repeatedly on hot backward branches\\nand calls even when their targets are immediate constants available at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small static predictor in IF that decodes only enough of io_imemData to\\nrecognize conditional branches with negative B-immediates and unconditional\\nJAL instructions. Fetch should set the next PC to the predicted target for\\nbackward branches and all JALs, carry the predicted next PC through ID/EX, and\\nlet EX redirect only when the actual next PC differs from the prediction.\\nCorrectly predicted loop backedges and JALs then avoid the two younger\\nwrong-path bubbles, while forward branches and JALR keep the existing\\ncorrection behavior. The added IF decode/adder is small compared with the\\ncurrent ALU/forwarding critical path, so the expected gain is primarily IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so EX can distinguish correct predictions from mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode branch/JAL immediates in fetch and choose the predicted next PC using a backward-taken, forward-not-taken static \n…[20362 of 23434 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0cccebcd0352a6b8]…\n8.1, \"fmax_mhz\": 37.625, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4446945, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2992, \"ff\": 708, \"seeds\": [36.488, 37.625, 37.625], \"perturbations\": [[0, 36.488, 26], [1, 37.625, 28], [2, 37.625, 28]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_27_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -22.406, \"arrival_ns\": 32.7, \"logic_cells\": 64, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 26, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T11:44:08.799545Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r3s2 (regression, -34.40%): Decode-side BTFN/JAL prediction still creates a long ID-to-IF PC-update feedback path through `imm` decode, target add, alignment, and stall/bubble gating, while EX `pred_next_pc` mismatch checks add control cost that CoreMark's saved taken-branch bubbles did not repay.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
