{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Single-entry last-target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The prior predictor attempts confirmed that CoreMark has useful taken direct\n  control flow, but they also showed that fetch-time immediate decode, target\n  adders, multi-entry BTB lookup, and decode-to-fetch redirects destroy Fmax on\n  this Tang Nano timing point. A predictor for this core needs to be almost\n  embarrassingly small and must reuse targets already computed by EX instead of\n  adding new target-generation logic to the front end.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry last-taken direct target predictor trained only by resolved\n  taken conditional branches and direct JALs in EX. The IF stage stores one\n  valid PC tag and one resolved target; on an exact current-PC hit it selects\n  the stored target instead of pc+4 and carries a predicted-next-PC flag/value\n  with the instruction. EX compares the resolved architectural next PC against\n  that carried value and redirects only on mismatch, invalidating the entry on a\n  not-taken branch at the tagged PC. This intentionally gives up broad BTB\n  coverage in exchange for a single compare, one target mux, no counters, no\n  fetch immediate decode, and no fetch target adder. It should catch the hottest\n  innermost CoreMark loop backedges and repeated direct jumps while avoiding the\n  large Fmax collapse seen in the 8-entry BTB and decode-side predictor.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact predicted-next-PC metadata to IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX/MEM-facing control so resolved EX can tell correct predictions from misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the single-entry exact-tag target predictor, use the stored target on a hit, and update or invalidate the entry from EX training signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted-next-PC metadata through decode without adding new decode-side branch target logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the predictor from resolved taken direct branches/JALs, invalidate on matching not-taken branches, and redirect only when the carried prediction differs from the actual next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor metadata and EX training signals between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the existing nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
