{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r5s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Tiny return-address-stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts for this core all lost because they placed target\n  generation, tag lookup, counters, or prediction mismatch plumbing on the\n  already fragile fetch/decode/execute feedback path. CoreMark still contains\n  call/return control flow, but the next predictor should be much narrower:\n  predict only canonical returns where the target is already known from a\n  previously executed call, and avoid computing branch or jump immediates in\n  the front end.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small return-address stack, for example four entries, trained by\n  resolved calls that write x1 or x5 and used only for canonical return-form\n  JALR instructions such as JALR x0, x1, 0 or JALR x0, x5, 0. Decode can\n  recognize this return pattern, redirect fetch to the current stack top, and\n  carry a predicted-next-PC bit/value into EX. EX still computes the true JALR\n  target, suppresses the normal redirect when the stack prediction was correct,\n  and repairs control flow on a mismatch. The stack is popped only when the\n  return reaches EX so speculative decode redirects do not corrupt it.\n\n  This does not help conditional loop backedges, but it deliberately avoids\n  the failed predictor ingredients: no BTB tag array, no fetch-time immediate\n  decode, no branch target adder, and no broad taken/not-taken predictor on\n  the fetch PC recurrence. If CoreMark has enough non-inlined calls, saving\n  one EX-resolution cycle on returns should improve iterations per cycle with\n  a much smaller Fmax penalty than the previous predictor designs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the ID/EX bundle for return predictions only.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the small return-address stack, canonical return detection, decode-time return redirect output, and predicted-next-PC latching.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the stack on resolved calls, pop on resolved returns, and suppress JALR redirects when the carried return prediction matches the actual target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept a decode-time return redirect that flushes queued sequential instructions and restarts fetch at the stack target.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire return prediction, stack training, and prediction metadata between ID, EX, and IF without changing the nret=1 top-level IO.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
