{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Queued-entry static branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts found useful CoreMark control-flow opportunities but\n  repeatedly lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC because target adders, tag\n  compares, counters, or decode redirects landed on the fetch PC feedback path.\n  The current champion already has a two-entry IF FIFO, and its queued entries\n  give a place to do small static branch predecode after fetch without changing\n  the zero-wait bypass PC recurrence.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add prediction metadata only to instructions that are captured into the IF\n  FIFO, not to the direct empty-FIFO bypass path. On each FIFO push, predecode\n  the fetched instruction into a registered predicted-next-PC for backward\n  conditional branches and direct JALs, enabling the prediction only when the\n  computed target is word-aligned. When decode later pops a FIFO head with a\n  taken prediction, IF flushes younger queued sequential instructions and\n  restarts fetch from the registered target. The predicted next PC is carried\n  through ID/EX so EX suppresses the normal redirect when the prediction was\n  correct and redirects to the resolved architectural next PC on a miss.\n\n  This deliberately gives up predictions for bypassed instructions and all\n  JALR/return cases, but it avoids the failed ingredients from earlier rounds:\n  no BTB tag lookup, no counter table, no fetch-time target adder in the active\n  PC select loop, and no decode-side target calculation. CoreMark's dmem stalls,\n  load-use bubbles, and RV32M busy cycles often let hot loop branches sit in the\n  IF queue, so this should recover taken-backedge bubbles from those queued\n  branches with a smaller Fmax penalty than previous predictor designs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact pred_valid and pred_next_pc fields to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so queued predictions can be verified in EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Predecode FIFO pushes for backward branches and direct JALs, store registered predicted targets per FIFO entry, and redirect only when a predicted FIFO head is popped.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the queued prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction without adding new decode-side target calculation.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the carried predicted next PC with the resolved architectural next PC and suppress the existing redirect only on correct queued predictions.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the prediction metadata through the existing nret=1 pipeline while keeping the top-level IO contract unchanged.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
