{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-003-r7s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description), \\\"---notes---\\\", .implementation_notes' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-003-r7s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description), \\\"---notes---\\\", .implementation_notes' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"Add a zero-table static predictor for direct JAL only at the decode\nboundary. When the IF/ID instruction is a valid JAL that decode will accept\nthis cycle, compute the aligned target as pc plus the existing J-immediate\nand redirect the IF stage immediately, flushing only younger queued fetch\nentries. Carry a single \"direct JAL already redirected\" bit into ID/EX so\nEX still produces the architectural pc_next and rd=pc+4 value, but\nsuppresses its normal later redirect for that same JAL. Misaligned JAL\ntargets, JALR, and all conditional branches keep the existing EX-resolution\nbehavior.\n\nThis should recover one redirect cycle for calls and direct jumps without\nreintroducing the failed ingredients from earlier predictor attempts: no\nBTB lookup, no branch-direction table, no RAS, no conditional branch target\npredecode, and no full predicted-next-PC mismatch compare. The risk is the\nnew ID-to-IF target-adder path, but limiting it to accepted direct JALs\nshould keep the timing cost much smaller than previous predictor designs.\n\n---\nrtl/core_pkg.sv: Add a one-bit ID/EX flag marking direct JAL instructions whose fetch redirect was already performed in decode.\nrtl/id_stage.sv: Recognize accepted direct JALs, reuse the decoded J-immediate to form an aligned early target, and latch the already-redirected flag.\nrtl/if_stage.sv: Accept a decode-stage direct-JAL redirect that clears younger queued entries and restarts fetch at the supplied target without changing the two-entry FIFO policy.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv: Suppress the normal EX redirect for direct JALs that were already redirected in decode while preserving RVFI pc_next and link-register writeback.\nrtl/core.sv: Wire the decode-stage direct-JAL redirect and the ID/EX already-redirected metadata through the existing nret=1 core.\n---notes---\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
