{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r9s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Word-aligned direct-JAL decode predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that the bench core cannot afford general\n  front-end prediction: BTBs, BTFN branch prediction, return stacks, and\n  queued prediction metadata all lengthened the fragile IF/redirect timing\n  boundary. The only predictor that came close was the narrow ID-stage\n  direct-JAL redirect, which improved measured fitness by about 4% but missed\n  the replacement threshold because the ID-to-IF target-add/alignment path was\n  still expensive.\nhypothesis: |\n  Revisit only that near-miss direct-JAL predictor, but make the decode redirect\n  cheaper instead of broader. For an accepted JAL, detect word alignment from\n  the instruction encoding before the full adder: with aligned PCs and JAL's\n  implicit bit zero, a valid RV32I word-aligned target has target[1] equal to\n  instr[21]. Gate the early redirect on instr[21] == 0, and form the redirect\n  address as {pc[31:2] + j_imm[31:2], 2'b00} so decode does not build or check a\n  full 32-bit byte target on the timing-critical ID-to-IF path.\n\n  Carry only a one-bit \"direct JAL already redirected\" marker into EX, not the\n  target. EX still computes the architectural JAL pc_next and link value on its\n  existing path, suppressing only the duplicate redirect for marked direct JALs.\n  JALR and conditional branches stay on the current EX-resolution path. This\n  keeps the single promising predictor case, removes target-carry metadata from\n  the failed follow-up, and should recover enough Fmax over the previous\n  direct-JAL near miss to clear the tournament threshold while preserving the\n  nret=1 RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add one ID/EX metadata bit indicating that an accepted direct JAL already performed its fetch redirect in decode.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize accepted direct JALs, gate early redirects with instr[21] for word alignment, and compute the redirect with a 30-bit word-address adder.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept the decode-stage direct-JAL redirect target, flush younger queued sequential entries, and restart fetch without adding BTB or branch-direction state.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the duplicate EX redirect for marked early direct JALs while keeping existing architectural pc_next, link-register writeback, and misalignment trapping.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the narrow decode-stage direct-JAL redirect and one-bit metadata through the existing single-retire pipeline.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
